{"name":"Mulled Wine","hex":"#524d5b","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"mulled wine","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["Red wine with spices (e.g. cinnamon sticks, cloves and ginger) served hot."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/mulled_wine"}],"entries":[{"title":"Mulled wine","blocks":[{"text":"Mulled wine, also known as spiced wine, is an alcoholic drink usually made with red wine, along with various mulling spices and sometimes raisins, served hot or warm. It is a traditional drink during winter, especially around Christmas. It is usually served at Christmas markets in Europe. There are non-alcoholic versions of it."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/7/77/Gl%C3%BChwein_Weinnachtsmarkt_OS.JPG/330px-Gl%C3%BChwein_Weinnachtsmarkt_OS.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Mulled_wine","wikidata":"Q6584"},{"title":"Wine","blocks":[{"text":"Wine is an alcoholic drink made from fermented grape juice. It is produced and consumed in many regions around the world, in a wide variety of styles which are influenced by different varieties of grapes, growing environments, viticulture methods, and production techniques."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/a/af/Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg/330px-Red_and_white_wine_in_glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine","wikidata":"Q282"},{"title":"Wine red","blocks":[{"text":"The color wine, or wine red, also called bordeaux, vinous, or vinaceous, is a dark shade of red and brown. It is a representation of the typical color of red wine."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/thumb/c/c0/Red_Wine_Glass.jpg/330px-Red_Wine_Glass.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Wine_red","wikidata":"Q3014419"}],"ima